{"title":"Daniele Antonioli Blog","url":"https://francozappa.github.io/","favicon":"https://francozappa.github.io/media/icon_hufd6449924b8771808a89b636be1cd7b0_295644_32x32_fill_lanczos_center_3.png","elements":[{"title":"The Zen of Bluetooth Security (ZOBS)","contents":"<div class=\"media-body\">\n\n    <div class=\"section-subheading article-title mb-0 mt-0\">\n      <a href=\"/post/2026/zobs-init/\">The Zen of Bluetooth Security (ZOBS)</a>\n    </div>\n\n    \n    <a href=\"/post/2026/zobs-init/\" class=\"summary-link\">\n      <div class=\"article-style\">\n        Recently, I presented the ZOBS principles in a keynote at ACM WiSec'26. Thanks again to Vincent Lenders and Gerhard Hancke for the invitation!\nKeynote abstract:\nThe Zen of Bluetooth Security (ZOBS) is a collection of Bluetooth security principles developed by the speaker to systematize seven years of research on Bluetooth security protocols.\n      </div>\n    </a>\n    \n\n    <div class=\"stream-meta article-metadata\">\n\n      \n\n      \n        \n\n\n<div class=\"article-metadata\">\n\n  \n  \n\n  \n  <span class=\"article-date\">\n    \n    \n      \n    \n    Jul 15, 2026\n  </span>\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n  <span class=\"middot-divider\"></span>\n  <span class=\"article-reading-time\">\n    2 min read\n  </span>\n  \n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n  \n  \n\n</div>\n\n      \n    </div>\n\n    \n\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ml-3\">\n    \n    \n    \n    <a href=\"/post/2026/zobs-init/\">\n      <img src=\"/post/2026/zobs-init/featured_huad29966f2e34c98bfc6a015972683a91_31342_150x0_resize_q75_h2_lanczos.webp\" height=\"149\" width=\"150\" alt=\"The Zen of Bluetooth Security (ZOBS)\" loading=\"lazy\">\n    </a>\n    \n  </div>","link":"https://francozappa.github.io/post/2026/zobs-init/","retrieved":1784073600000},{"title":"BLERP Peripheral Impersonation Attack Demo","contents":"<div class=\"media-body\">\n\n    <div class=\"section-subheading article-title mb-0 mt-0\">\n      <a href=\"/post/2026/blerp-pidemo/\">BLERP Peripheral Impersonation Attack Demo</a>\n    </div>\n\n    \n    <a href=\"/post/2026/blerp-pidemo/\" class=\"summary-link\">\n      <div class=\"article-style\">\n        Here is Tommaso Sacchetti demonstrating the BLERP peripheral impersonation attack against a vulnerable Android 13 build (2024). In this setup, an attacker in proximity impersonates a trusted mouse, triggers an unauthenticated re-pairing, and takes over the input channel.\n      </div>\n    </a>\n    \n\n    <div class=\"stream-meta article-metadata\">\n\n      \n\n      \n        \n\n\n<div class=\"article-metadata\">\n\n  \n  \n\n  \n  <span class=\"article-date\">\n    \n    \n      \n    \n    Mar 23, 2026\n  </span>\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n  <span class=\"middot-divider\"></span>\n  <span class=\"article-reading-time\">\n    1 min read\n  </span>\n  \n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n  \n  \n\n</div>\n\n      \n    </div>\n\n    \n\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ml-3\">\n    \n    \n    \n    <a href=\"/post/2026/blerp-pidemo/\">\n      <img src=\"/post/2026/blerp-pidemo/featured_hu892df9b508019aa35ba9a2a75756df7d_108557_150x0_resize_q75_h2_lanczos.webp\" height=\"173\" width=\"150\" alt=\"BLERP Peripheral Impersonation Attack Demo\" loading=\"lazy\">\n    </a>\n    \n  </div>","link":"https://francozappa.github.io/post/2026/blerp-pidemo/","retrieved":1774224000000},{"title":"E-Trojans Black Hat USA 25 Video","contents":"<div class=\"media-body\">\n\n    <div class=\"section-subheading article-title mb-0 mt-0\">\n      <a href=\"/post/2026/etro-bhusa/\">E-Trojans Black Hat USA 25 Video</a>\n    </div>\n\n    \n    <a href=\"/post/2026/etro-bhusa/\" class=\"summary-link\">\n      <div class=\"article-style\">\n        Last summer, Marco Casagrande and I talked about E-Trojans: Ransomware, Tracking, DoS, and Data Leaks on Xiaomi Electric Scooters at Black Hat USA 2025. Our presentation is online:\n      </div>\n    </a>\n    \n\n    <div class=\"stream-meta article-metadata\">\n\n      \n\n      \n        \n\n\n<div class=\"article-metadata\">\n\n  \n  \n\n  \n  <span class=\"article-date\">\n    \n    \n      \n    \n    Mar 18, 2026\n  </span>\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n  <span class=\"middot-divider\"></span>\n  <span class=\"article-reading-time\">\n    1 min read\n  </span>\n  \n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n  \n  \n\n</div>\n\n      \n    </div>\n\n    \n\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ml-3\">\n    \n    \n    \n    <a href=\"/post/2026/etro-bhusa/\">\n      <img src=\"/post/2026/etro-bhusa/featured_huf50a79a25c883e89886b5ee6b7e78de9_34040_150x0_resize_q75_h2_lanczos.webp\" height=\"67\" width=\"150\" alt=\"E-Trojans Black Hat USA 25 Video\" loading=\"lazy\">\n    </a>\n    \n  </div>","link":"https://francozappa.github.io/post/2026/etro-bhusa/","retrieved":1773792000000},{"title":"DCS-CI: Design for Cyber Secure Critical Infra","contents":"<div class=\"media-body\">\n\n    <div class=\"section-subheading article-title mb-0 mt-0\">\n      <a href=\"/post/2026/dcsci-cfp/\">DCS-CI: Design for Cyber Secure Critical Infra</a>\n    </div>\n\n    \n    <a href=\"/post/2026/dcsci-cfp/\" class=\"summary-link\">\n      <div class=\"article-style\">\n        The call for submission for the first edition of the DCS-CI conference is online.\nThe Design of Cyber-Secure Critical Infrastructure (DCS-CI) 26 conference invites researchers, practitioners, and thought leaders to submit original work that advances our collective understanding of how to design, deploy, and maintain secure critical infrastructure systems.\n      </div>\n    </a>\n    \n\n    <div class=\"stream-meta article-metadata\">\n\n      \n\n      \n        \n\n\n<div class=\"article-metadata\">\n\n  \n  \n\n  \n  <span class=\"article-date\">\n    \n    \n      \n    \n    Mar 16, 2026\n  </span>\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n  <span class=\"middot-divider\"></span>\n  <span class=\"article-reading-time\">\n    1 min read\n  </span>\n  \n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n  \n  \n\n</div>\n\n      \n    </div>\n\n    \n\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ml-3\">\n    \n    \n    \n    <a href=\"/post/2026/dcsci-cfp/\">\n      <img src=\"/post/2026/dcsci-cfp/featured_hube2d1528fa0e62d4bc34aad6d13bcd9e_235699_150x0_resize_q75_h2_lanczos_3.webp\" height=\"76\" width=\"150\" alt=\"DCS-CI: Design for Cyber Secure Critical Infra\" loading=\"lazy\">\n    </a>\n    \n  </div>","link":"https://francozappa.github.io/post/2026/dcsci-cfp/","retrieved":1773619200000},{"title":"WiSec'26 Call for Posters and Demos","contents":"<div class=\"media-body\">\n\n    <div class=\"section-subheading article-title mb-0 mt-0\">\n      <a href=\"/post/2026/wisec-pd/\">WiSec'26 Call for Posters and Demos</a>\n    </div>\n\n    \n    <a href=\"/post/2026/wisec-pd/\" class=\"summary-link\">\n      <div class=\"article-style\">\n        I am excited to chair the WiSec Demo and Poster session.\nPlease submit your great posters and demos via this HotCRP instance!\nAll poster titles must be prefixed with POSTER: and all demo titles with DEMO:.\n      </div>\n    </a>\n    \n\n    <div class=\"stream-meta article-metadata\">\n\n      \n\n      \n        \n\n\n<div class=\"article-metadata\">\n\n  \n  \n\n  \n  <span class=\"article-date\">\n    \n    \n      \n    \n    Mar 16, 2026\n  </span>\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n  <span class=\"middot-divider\"></span>\n  <span class=\"article-reading-time\">\n    1 min read\n  </span>\n  \n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n  \n  \n\n</div>\n\n      \n    </div>\n\n    \n\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ml-3\">\n    \n    \n    \n    <a href=\"/post/2026/wisec-pd/\">\n      <img src=\"/post/2026/wisec-pd/featured_huc1b3513e5829618ed2bb7677e18cff27_1338018_150x0_resize_q75_h2_lanczos_3.webp\" height=\"53\" width=\"150\" alt=\"WiSec'26 Call for Posters and Demos\" loading=\"lazy\">\n    </a>\n    \n  </div>","link":"https://francozappa.github.io/post/2026/wisec-pd/","retrieved":1773619200000}]}